{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "notes": "Boot an NBA Fastbreak ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape, wait out the power-up mechanism test, open the service menu and start T.1 SWITCH EDGES, then set every public matrix address 11-88 and every Fliptronic address 111-118 to 1 and back to 0 in turn, holding each level for 2 s. The ROM's top display line names a switch while it reads it as active, so the edge that brings a name up shows which public level the ROM treats as active, and the name it prints is the ROM's own label for that address.",
